Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 20:08:02 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 29/31] Tests: EPA's horizon loop test and the restart after a
 scan that is not one loop

test_horizon_is_loop runs _horizon_is_loop on synthetic horizons: one loop in any edge order, figure-8s through the walk's start vertex and through another vertex (one in an edge order where a walk that does not reject a vertex on four horizon edges uses all edges before it closes), two disjoint loops, an open path, fewer than 3 edges and an overflowed buffer.

test_epa_nonloop_horizon: three poses (two stacked 5 cm boxes, two ellipsoids; MetalSim epa-review) on which EPA's face scan, with the full-size horizon buffer, leaves a horizon that is not one loop, so the scan is undone and the region grows from the closest face. The deepest contact matches MuJoCo C's (2e-8 m for the boxes, the ccd tolerance for the ellipsoids) with no overflow bit. The face scan alone (93e5ce1) gives the same contacts on these poses, so the test pins the restart path rather than a change of result: a restart that drops the contact fails it.
